{
  "table_id": "Table_S23C",
  "display_number": "S23",
  "title": "Supplementary Table S23. Attrition sensitivity analyses.",
  "panel": "C",
  "panel_title": "Panel c. Pattern-mixture difference-in-differences estimates by non-ignorable attrition parameter δ (N = 8,365 observations).",
  "notes_before": [],
  "notes_after": [
    "Note. For each 2011-only participant with complete model covariates (947 of 1,757), a 2015 observation was imputed as baseline BAA + d̄ + δ, where d̄ = −0.212 years is the mean within-person BAA change among completers and δ indexes increasingly adverse non-ignorable attrition. Exposure groups used analytical-sample median cutpoints of 4-year-average exposures (1 km: EVI 0.3442, O₃ 84.028; 500 m: EVI 0.3135, O₃ 83.823). The augmented cohort (N = 8,365 observations) was re-analysed with an unweighted joint mixed model (exposure weights are not defined for the imputed attriter rows); the δ = 0 run serves as the internal reference. BAA used the recalibrated PhenoAge scale (correlation ~0.68 with the primary-analysis BAA).",
    "Abbreviations: BAA, biological age acceleration; CI, confidence interval; DiD, difference-in-differences; EVI, enhanced vegetation index; IPAW, inverse-probability-of-attrition weighting; O₃, ozone; SD, standard deviation."
  ],
